  "inSpec": true,
  "text": "Using the data from Figure A, complete Figure B by:\n(i) plotting the data for Egypt, Iran and the Czech Republic.\n(ii) drawing a regression (best-fit) line to show the relationship.\n*S49795A01524* Pearson Edexcel Level 3 Advanced GCE in Geography – Sample Assessment Materials – 15\n79\nIssue 2 – February 2017 © Pearson Education Limited 2017\n0.5 Nigeria\nGini Coe cient Malawi\n0.4\nUnited\nStates\n0.3 India France\nNorway\n0.2\n0.4 0.5 0.6 0.7 0.9 0.9 1.0\nHuman Development Index\nFigure B: Graph showing the Human Development Index and the Gini Coefficient\nscores for selected countries\n(b) Suggest reasons for the relationship between Human Development Index and\nGini Coefficient scores.\n*S49795A01624* 16\n80\nPearson Edexcel Level 3 Advanced GCE in Geography – Sample Assessment Materials –\nIssue 2 – February 2017 © Pearson Education Limited 2017",
  "ms": "Answer Mark\nnumber (3)\nAO3 (3 marks)\nAward 1 mark for each correctly plotted point for Egypt, Iran and\nthe Czech Republic, up to maximum of 3 marks.\nAnswer Mark\nnumber (1)\nAO3 (1 mark)\nAward 1 mark for a line of best fit that falls within the acceptable\nrange shown below.\n116 Pearson Edexcel Level 3 Advanced GCE in Geography – Sample Assessment Materials –\nIssue 2 – February 2017 © Pearson Education Limited 2017",
