  "inSpec": false,
  "text": "Explain why some urban locations are perceived as undesirable by some groups.\n Turn over",
  "ms": "Explain why some urban locations are perceived as undesirable by some\nnumber groups.\nAnswer\nAO1 (6 marks)\n• Some urban locations such as London are perceived as undesirable due to\nhigh living costs particularly the high cost of housing resulting in first time\nbuyers being unable to afford properties.\n• Some areas’ environmental quality has changed over time which can led\npeople to view them as undesirable (industrialisation/deindustrialisation)\n• Areas with low environmental quality particularly in inner city areas where\nthere is substandard housing, atmospheric pollution and noise and light\npollution.\n• Urban locations with particularly high levels of crime and antisocial\nbehaviour are seen to be undesirable due to concerns of over safety and\nwellbeing.\n• The perception of the desirability of an area depends on a range of factors,\ninclude ethnicity, age and gender, as well as the lived experience of the\nindividual.\nAccept any other appropriate response.\nLevel Mark Descriptor\nLevel 1 0 No rewardable material.\nLevel 2 1–2\nLevel 3 • Demonstrates isolated elements of geographical knowledge and\n3–4 understanding, some of which may be inaccurate or irrelevant.\n5–6 (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a narrow range of geographical ideas,\nwhich lack detail. (AO1)\n• Demonstrates geographical knowledge and understanding, which\nis mostly relevant and may include some inaccuracies. (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a range of geographical ideas, which are\nnot fully detailed and/or developed. (AO1)\n• Demonstrates accurate and relevant geographical knowledge and\nunderstanding throughout. (AO1)\n• Understanding addresses a broad range of geographical ideas,\nwhich are detailed and fully developed. (AO1)",
