  "topic": "geo-syn",
  "topicConfident": true,
  "inSpec": true,
  "text": "The table below shows data on income per capita and tropical rainforest forest\ncover loss for 10 countries.\nThe formula for Spearman’s rank correlation coefficient value R is given below.\nR = 1 - 6∑d2\nn3- n\nComplete the table below and calculate the value of R for the data given.\nShow your working.\nCountry Income Rank % forest Rank d\nBrunei per capita cover loss 7 d2\n(2014 US$) 1990–2005 1\n1\n36,600 1 11.2 1\n1\nCosta Rica 10,000 4 29.4 3 2\n2 4\nIndonesia 3,500 6 30.8 2 1 4\n1 1\nKenya 1,400 8 5.1 9 1\nƩ\nMadagascar 450 10 1.5 10\nMexico 10,700 3 15.3 5\nPanama 11,100 2 18.0 4\nPapua New Guinea 2,100 7 13.7 6\nSenegal 1,000 9 9.2 8\nSri Lanka 3,600 5 35.0 1\nR = ..............................................................\n*S49796A0312* Pearson Edexcel Level 3 Advanced GCE in Geography – Sample Assessment Materials – 3\n135\nIssue 2 – February 2017 © Pearson Education Limited 2017",
  "ms": "Indicative content Mark\nnumber (4)\nAO3 (4 marks)\nAward 1 mark for completion of empty d and d2 rows:\n6 36\n4 16\n0 0\n4 16\nAward 1 mark for the sum of d2 column (Σ) = 80\nAward 1 mark for the correct working of equation:\n6 x 80 480\n1 − 10! − 10 𝐨𝐨𝐨𝐨𝐨𝐨𝐨𝐨 1 − 990 = R\nAward 1 mark for answers that round to R = 0.52\nOR\nAward full marks for the correct value of R alone.\nAllow error carried forward from each step.\nPearson Edexcel Level 3 Advanced GCE in Geography – Sample Assessment Materials – 157\nIssue 2 – February 2017 © Pearson Education Limited 2017",
  "pageFrom": 3,
  "pageTo": 3,
  "pdf": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 3 (Synoptic)/Questions/Specimen QP.pdf",
  "rb": "Exam questions PDFs/A-Level Geography/Paper 3 (Synoptic)/Resource Booklet/Specimen RB.pdf",
  "rbFrom": null,
  "rbTo": null,
  "rbMissing": false
