  "topic": "geo-syn",
  "topicConfident": true,
  "inSpec": true,
  "text": "The table on the next page shows data for the 12 richest countries (measured\nusing GDP per capita).\nThe formula for Spearman’s rank correlation coefficient is given below.\n6 ∑ d2\nR = 1 -\nn3 - n\nComplete the table below and calculate the value of R to two decimal places\nwhere n=12.\nCountry (population size GDP per Rank Military Rank d d2\nin millions) capita in 10 spending as 4\na % of GDP 6 36\nUnited States (324.5) $US\n5.7\n57,436\nSaudi Arabia (32.9) 55,158 11 15.2 1 10 100\nNetherlands (17.0) 51,049 12 2.8 939\nUnited Arab Emirates (9.4) 67,871 8 5.0 539\nSwitzerland (8.4) 59,561 9 1.7 10 -1 1\nSingapore (5.7) 87,855 3 4.8 6 -3 9\nNorway (5.3) 69,249 6 2.9 8 -2 4\nIreland (4.7) 69,231 7 0.6 12 -5 25\nKuwait (4.1) 71,887 5 8.2 239\nQatar (2.6) 127,660 1 3.2 7 -6 36\nLuxembourg (0.6) 104,003 2 1.1 11 -9 81\nBrunei (0.4) 76,884 4 6.6 311\nΣd2 =\nTable 1\nMilitary spending as a % of GDP for the 12 richest countries, as measured by\ntheir GDP per capita\nShow your working. Give your answer to two decimal places.\nR = ..............................................................",
  "ms": "Mark\nThe table below shows data for the 12 richest countries\n(measured using GDP (per capita).\nThe formula for Spearman’s rank correlation\ncoefficient is given below.\nComplete the table below and calculate the value of R\nfor the data given, to two decimal places.\nShow your working.\n(4)\nIndicative content\nAO3 (4 marks) (4)\nCountry (population size in GDP per Rank Military Rank d d 2\nmillions) capita in spending\n$US 10 as a % of 4 6 36\nUnited States(324.5) 11 GDP 1 10 100\nSaudi Arabia (32.9) 57,436 12 9\nNetherlands (17.0) 55,158 5.7 5 3 9\nUAE (9.4) 51,049 8 15.2 10 3 9\nSwitzerland (8.4) 67,871 9 6 -1 1\nSingapore (5.7) 59,561 3 2.8 8 -3 9\nNorway (5.3) 87,855 6 5.0 12 -2 4\nIreland (4.7) 69,249 7 1.7 2 -5 25\nKuwait (4.1) 69,231 5 4.8 7 3 9\nQatar (2.6) 71,887 1 2.9 11 -6 36\nLuxembourg (0.6) 127,660 2 0.6 3 -9 81\nBrunei (0.4) 104,003 4 8.2 1 1\n76,884 3.2 320\n1.1 d 2\n6.6\nUp to 3 marks for any of the following\n1 mark for correct addition of d2 = 320\n1 mark for correct calculation of 6x320 = 1920\n1 mark for correct substitution of n3 – n = 123 – 12 or 1728 -12 or result 1716\n1 mark for 1- 320/286\n1 mark for – 17/143\n1 mark for unrounded answer = -0.118881 or similar\nAnd a final 4th mark for correct result to two decimal places of -0.12\nIf error made do not double penalise if that error is carried forward – for\nexample if 6x320 is wrongly calculated credit result if correctly calculated from\nthe candidates figure(s).",
